grund config — inspect the effective `grund.toml` discovered from a path.

Usage:  grund config <show | validate> [PATH]
        grund config explain [TARGET] [PATH] [--path PATH] [--codes | --all]
        grund config migrate --to 2 [PATH] [--write] [--drop-comments] [--full]

  show       print the effective config as TOML in the file's own version (defaults filled in for keys you didn't set).
  validate   parse the discovered config and report the first error; exit 0 if it's well-formed.
  explain    say what a table, a key or a check code is, in the version the file is read as; with no target, list
             the tables. It reads the file's version and nothing else, so a config other commands refuse is answered.
  migrate    preview the version-2 file that means what this version-1 config means, and report where each key went;
             writes nothing unless --write is given; successful writes use a compact report.

Options:
  --codes              explain: every check code the version can report, one line each.
                       e.g. grund config explain --codes
  --all                explain: every table with its keys, then every check code.
                       e.g. grund config explain --all
  --path PATH          explain: the path to discover the config from, so the first positional stays the target.
                       e.g. grund config explain oversized-lead --path docs/
  --to 2               migrate: the version to migrate to; required, and 2 is the only one.
                       e.g. grund config migrate --to 2
  --write              migrate: replace the config with the candidate, once both comparisons pass.
                       e.g. grund config migrate --to 2 --write
  --full               migrate: restore the candidate on stdout and complete report on stderr after a successful write.
                       e.g. grund config migrate --to 2 --write --full
  --drop-comments      migrate: let --write drop the comments the preview lists, and name them again.
                       e.g. grund config migrate --to 2 --write --drop-comments
  --path-base project|invocation
                       project (default) spells report paths from the config root;
                       invocation: relative to the path you passed, or the current directory if you passed none.
                       e.g. grund config show docs/ --path-base=invocation
                       --path-base=invocation replaces a version-1 `[output] relative_paths = false`.

PATH defaults to `.`; config is discovered by walking up from it — the root `grund.toml` is the home, `.agents/grund.toml` a deprecated fallback.
There is no `--config <file>` override: it is discovered, not pointed at.

Exit:  0 well-formed / printed / answered / migrated · 1 `validate` found an error, `explain` knows no such target, or `migrate` refused · 2 no subcommand, or the config couldn't be read.

Examples:
  grund config show               # the effective config, defaults filled in
  grund config validate           # exit 1 if the discovered config has an error
  grund config show docs/         # the config that governs docs/
  grund config explain oversized-lead   # what a check code means, its severity and what turns it on
  grund config explain '[schema.sources]'           # a table: its keys, bracketed as in the file
  grund config explain '[schema.sources] exclude'   # one key of a table, after its bracketed header
  grund config migrate --to 2     # the version-2 file, previewed; nothing written
  grund config migrate --to 2 --write   # compact report on stderr; stdout is empty
  grund config migrate --to 2 --write --full   # apply with candidate and complete report

Guide:    https://github.com/agent-grounds/grund/blob/main/docs/user-facing/explain.md
Guide:    https://github.com/agent-grounds/grund/blob/main/docs/user-facing/migrating.md
Example:  https://github.com/agent-grounds/grund/tree/main/examples/config-explain
Example:  https://github.com/agent-grounds/grund/tree/main/examples/migrate
